"The shapes @asConnection does not expand, stated as the rows that are absent. The expansion admits a bare list of a named type and nothing else, so a list of lists and a field that is not a list at all carry the application and mint nothing; the carrier relation is where that verdict lives, and a field missing from it is the whole of it. The admitted carrier beside them is the control: an empty carrier relation would pass this document whether the rule worked or not."
type Film @table(name: "film") { id: ID }

extend type Query {
  admitted: [Film!]! @asConnection
  nested: [[Film!]!]! @asConnection
  single: Film @asConnection
}

extend schema @expectEquals(relation: "graphitron_connection_carrier", rows: """
  type_name, field_name, connection_name
  Query,     admitted,   QueryAdmittedConnection
  """)

extend schema @expectEquals(relation: "graphitron_type_minted", rows: """
  type_name
  QueryAdmittedConnection
  QueryAdmittedConnectionEdge
  PageInfo
  """)

extend schema @expectEquals(relation: "graphitron_argument_minted", rows: """
  type_name, field_name, argument_name
  Query,     admitted,   first
  Query,     admitted,   after
  """)
